# libnng for the two runtime identifiers nng.NET does not publish. scripts/build-nng.sh builds each
# one from nng's source, and the result is committed beside this file as native/<rid>/<file>.
#
# The package's other six (linux-x64, linux-arm64, linux-arm, osx-x64, win-x64, win-x86) are copied
# verbatim out of the nng.NET package; see src/KiCadSharp/KiCadSharp.csproj. Each build here pins the
# nng release that its platform's nng.NET binary is, so every Mac runs one nng and every Windows
# machine runs one nng, whatever the architecture:
#
#   osx-arm64  nng 1.3.2, as nng.NET's osx-x64 libnng.dylib is
#   win-arm64  nng 1.4.0, as nng.NET's win-x64 and win-x86 nng.dll are
#
# Each tag MUST be pinned to its commit: an upstream tag can be moved, and the script refuses to build
# from one that has been. The SHA-256 is that of the committed file, and the nng workflow fails unless
# a rebuild from this line reproduces it byte for byte.
#
# To move a pin: edit the line, run scripts/build-nng.sh <rid> on the matching host (or take the file
# the nng workflow uploads), and commit the new file and its SHA-256 together.
#
# rid       tag     commit                                    file          sha256
